\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces A seed-paired replication shows the per-window structure is real and largely reproducible, so the failure of the evaluated selectors is not explained by ``there is nothing there to learn''. The replication covers $48$ of the $127$ decision groups ($37.8\%$) on three backbones --- \texttt  {TimesNet} is absent --- and the reproducible share of headroom is heterogeneous across them: \texttt  {DLinear} $99.1\%$, \texttt  {PatchTST} $87.2\%$, \texttt  {iTransformer} $48.7\%$.}}{12}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:crossseed}{{11}{12}{A seed-paired replication shows the per-window structure is real and largely reproducible, so the failure of the evaluated selectors is not explained by ``there is nothing there to learn''. The replication covers $48$ of the $127$ decision groups ($37.8\%$) on three backbones --- \arm {TimesNet} is absent --- and the reproducible share of headroom is heterogeneous across them: \arm {DLinear} $99.1\%$, \arm {PatchTST} $87.2\%$, \arm {iTransformer} $48.7\%$}{table.11}{}}
